cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use proxy-scraper or its proxy snapshots in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "proxy-scraper: free proxies that actually work"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feix
    given-names: Maximilian
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper"
url: "https://maximilianfeix.github.io/proxy-scraper/"
abstract: >-
  proxy-scraper collects public HTTP, SOCKS4 and SOCKS5 proxies from 700+ sources and keeps only the ones that pass
  every check: a protocol handshake, the same exit IP on two unrelated sites (drops honeypots), a byte-for-byte
  content check (drops proxies that inject scripts) and, for HTTPS, a verified TLS handshake. It publishes a checked
  list every hour and a daily snapshot with exit IP, country, ASN, datacenter flag, anonymity, latency, speed,
  uptime and site reachability.
keywords:
  - proxies
  - open proxies
  - proxy checker
  - networking
  - web scraping
  - honeypot detection
